{"duration_api_ms":226204,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"68177dca-62fe-44d2-9735-0d0565510c48","total_cost_usd":0.265234,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13930,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15115},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13930,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":20951,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13930},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":20951,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13930,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.265234,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":15115,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 9 feasible non-dominated designs sit on one ridge: bluntness 1.2, cone 69.9 deg, D 3.3-3.38 m, entry angle -2.2 to -3.58 deg. Hypervolume is dominated by the bondline temperature axis, because flux is only about 0.1 of the 2.5 MW/m2 reference range while T spans 392-408 K of a 150 K range. The binding limit is max_g <= 12, reached at about -3.58 deg, and the heatshield mass-fraction margin runs out near D of about 3.385 m. In the data, T falls with steeper angle (about -10 K/deg), falls with larger D (about -18 K/m) and falls slightly with higher bluntness. Flux rises with steeper angle (about +24 kW/m2 per deg) and falls with larger D (about -120 kW/m2 per m). The ridge is therefore best pushed to D = 3.38 (the largest D with a verified positive mass margin) across the whole angle range.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3: D 3.38 has mass margin 0.003 (D 3.35: 0.0207, D 3.37: 0.0089), so D 3.38 is the largest verified buildable diameter; the extrapolated zero crossing is near 3.385.\",\"C-d8198ec304c5: D 3.33, -3.58 deg gives g = 11.994 (margin 0.0005) and T = 391.96 K. Fitting the 3.3 m rows (C-158e05f9d36e, C-5dab03f5d001, C-2cf973a097ba) gives dg/d|gamma| of about 1.65 per deg and dg/dD of about +0.38 per m.\",\"C-f07c60fdbdae vs C-0c6e47855b5e vs C-944b08da02c1: lowering bluntness from 1.2 to 1.1 raises T by about 0.65 K and flux by about 5 kW/m2 and lowers the mass margin, so b = 1.2 is best.\",\"C-bcce2808c9b8 and C-a554636d8035 (b 1.22-1.25) fail the cd_fore convex hull, and C-ed967979f72a (b 1.3, cone 69.9) fails geometry, so b > 1.2 is not reachable.\",\"C-404e4e066a3e and C-b76a72930094: the shallow end (-2.2, -2.4 deg) gives 246-250 kW/m2 at 405-408 K. Extending to -1.5 deg has not been tried.\",\"C-02335773e828, C-2d91d8d713d7 and C-c97855c2d790: steeper angles (-6 to -7.4 deg) reach lower T but have g of 16-19, so they are infeasible and not competitive.\"],\"mechanism\":\"This relies partly on prior Allen-Eggers-type reasoning, calibrated to local linear fits of the data. A larger D at fixed mass lowers the ballistic coefficient, so the vehicle decelerates higher in the atmosphere and its heat pulse is smaller. A larger nose radius (bluntness and D) lowers stagnation flux. A steeper angle shortens the heat pulse and lowers integrated load and bondline T, but raises peak g and flux. Peak g is set mainly by entry angle, with a weak D dependence, so the g <= 12 wall caps the steepness. Mass fraction depends on D, bluntness and cone angle but not on entry angle. The best achievable points therefore have D just under the mass limit, b = 1.2, cone near 70 deg, and entry angle chosen along the trade-off curve. I propose to shift the whole known front to D = 3.38 (about 0.5 K lower T and 3-4 kW/m2 lower flux at each angle), extend it shallow to -1.5 deg, and spend four slots probing bluntness and cone sensitivity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The linear fits for g, T and flux were calibrated on D 3.2-3.38 and s = 2.2-3.6. Predictions at -1.5 to -2.1 deg extrapolate beyond the measured shallow end, and T there may be off by a few K. The g margin at -3.55 deg is only about 0.2%, and I am relying on the fitted slope. The four exploratory points (lower cone or bluntness) may fail geometry or the hull check, since the buildable cone/bluntness boundary is only known coarsely. I have not used the higher-fidelity simulator, so high-fidelity effects such as real-gas heating and ablation are not represented.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"Steepest safe angle at D 3.38. Fitted g is about 11.97 (limit 12). This should give the lowest T on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the D 3.38 ridge reaches T of about 391.3 K, below the current best of 391.96 K, while staying under g = 12.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 version of the -3.5 deg front point. It should beat C-f07c60fdbdae (277.0 kW/m2, 392.38 K) in both objectives.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the D 3.38 improvement (about -0.5 K and -3.5 kW/m2) on a well-fitted part of the ridge.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 shift of the mid-steep front near -3.4 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the improved front. It should dominate C-5dab03f5d001 (280.6 kW/m2, 394.29 K) and C-4b29088b4edc.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 shift near -3.3 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the front point C-4b29088b4edc (272.2 kW/m2, 394.41 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at -3.1 deg. The angle lies between existing 3.35 m rows at -3.0 and -3.3 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front and slightly improves C-8995972bc17f (264.85 kW/m2, 397.67 K).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at -3.0 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":261300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the same-angle 3.35 m front point C-8995972bc17f in both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at -2.9 deg, in the middle of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Covers the mid-front gap between -2.7 and -3.0 deg with an improved-D design.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at -2.7 deg. It should improve on C-80e473c8a476 (D 3.3, 263.3 kW/m2, 402.19 K).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves both objectives at -2.7 deg through the larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at -2.5 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between -2.4 and -2.7 deg with the improved diameter.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at -2.3 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the shallow-end front points C-404e4e066a3e and C-b76a72930094.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 at -2.2 deg, same angle as the low-flux front point C-404e4e066a3e.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct A/B comparison against C-404e4e066a3e (245.77 kW/m2, 407.82 K) to confirm the D 3.35 to 3.38 gain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"Extends the front toward lower flux by going shallower than any evaluated point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Starts extrapolating beyond the measured shallow end, where the flux drop is worth adding to hypervolume.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower extension to -1.9 deg for lower flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether flux keeps falling linearly (about 23 kW/m2 per deg) toward shallow entry and whether T stays under 450 K.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow extension to -1.7 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":230700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the flux-versus-T curvature at shallow angles. This is the far-left end of the trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow extension to -1.6 deg, close to the bound.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes near the shallow limit, where the skip or shallow-entry behaviour of the reduced model is unknown.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"Shallowest allowed angle, -1.5 deg, giving the minimum-flux extreme of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":226100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Defines the low-flux end of the front. The gain is small but new area is added to the hypervolume.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0c6e47855b5e\",\"rationale\":\"Exploratory: lower the cone half-angle from 69.9 to 67.5 deg at b = 1.1 (which has more geometry room than b = 1.2) to see whether cone angle can lower T or g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cone sensitivity is unmeasured near the ridge (only 69.9 vs 70 tested). Learns whether the fore-cone geometry and hull permit lower angles here.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-944b08da02c1\",\"rationale\":\"Exploratory: moderate bluntness 1.0 with cone 66 deg, above the estimated geometry boundary, to check the bluntness trend for g and mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":292000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the bluntness trend (higher T and flux as b falls) and whether an off-ridge design gives any low-T alternative.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5dab03f5d001\",\"rationale\":\"Exploratory: far off-ridge low-bluntness design (b 0.7, cone 63 deg) at D 3.3 and -3.4 deg. It tests the previously unexplored low-b, moderate-cone region at a g-feasible angle.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":63.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":330000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"All feasible points so far are at b of about 1.1-1.2. Confirms the ridge is not beaten by lower-bluntness designs and maps the geometry boundary.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3dfb47a1c8a3\",\"rationale\":\"Exploratory: D 3.38, b 1.2 with the cone at 69.0 deg (vs 69.9) and -3.4 deg entry, to measure the cone slope at maximum bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cone angle near the geometry and hull limit at b = 1.2 has not been tested. Learns the sensitivity and boundary distance.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":175675,"type":"result","duration_ms":226237,"uuid":"bf41ed38-a57d-48f1-83cb-5d1431b9b190","ttft_stream_ms":1383,"time_to_request_ms":31,"first_content_frame_ms":1383,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
